# A day on which nothing runs.
#
# 2026-09-12 is a Saturday. The bus service in this slice runs Fridays and the
# rail service runs weekdays, so both counts are zero and every list is empty.
#
# This is the shape a stale cache takes, and the shape a wrong service-date
# calculation takes, and the shape a correct app takes on a real holiday. They
# are indistinguishable from inside, which is why what the app draws here has
# to be written down: zero routes on both modes, an empty list under each, and
# a search that finds nothing rather than finding stops nothing calls at.
cache ../cache.db
date 2026-09-12
time 08:00
offset -04:00
size 100 14

# Both modes, each with nothing under it.
enter
esc
down
enter
esc

# And a search. The stops are still in the cache -- it is the service that is
# not running -- so an implementation that searched stops without asking what
# calls there would list them happily.
type billings
